WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's been very strange for you
doing press recently,

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of "Star Wars,"
obviously.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.438
You don't want to talk to people
too much about it.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:06.306 line:92%
They don't want you to ruin it.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:08.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know you're going to do
another season of

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.275 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Big Little Lies."

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
You really probably can't talk
about that that much.

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:12.379 line:92%
"Twin Peaks" you haven't --

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
Has that been strange to do
press for projects

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:15.348 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that are so under wraps?

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:18.351
-I'm the most boring interview,
I think, possible.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:18.918 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's not true.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.821
-Thank you for having me here,
because I can't say a thing.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.657
I mean, literally, I can't wait
for everyone to see "Star Wars,"

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
because all I can say is,
yes, I can confirm

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.261 line:92%
I have purple hair in the film.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:28.895 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, there you go.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's nice of you to confirm
that much for us.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:34.968 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's a great color.
I recommend it.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:40.273
-Did they let you give them
feedback on the color of purple?

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Oh, they did?

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's nice.
-Yeah.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:44.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
-See? You have a successful
enough career,

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they let you
choose your purple.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Isn't that beautiful? Yeah.
-That's well-deserved.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:52.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is your family
excited about "Star Wars"?

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.820 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Either generation?

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They are. Everybody.
-Yeah.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, my kids --
I'm thrilled that my kids

00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:01.127
are actually going to get
to see me in something.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:01.961 line:92%
I can talk about the film.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:05.965
Not that you don't start kids on
David Lynch at like age 5.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:06.766 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But I haven't.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:07.434 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Your kids are like,

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:10.570
"I have a lot of questions about
'Wild at Heart.'"

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:11.171 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:14.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
But my parents took me to see
"Star Wars"

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.408 size:84% position:42% line:92%
when I was 7 years old.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:16.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's --
-Yeah.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, we're all obsessed,
aren't we?

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.380 line:92%
It is a cultural phenomenon.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.314 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-And this is a photo --

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.583 size:78% position:39%
I am assuming this is
from the premiere.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:26.619
Is that accurate?
-Yes. From our press in London.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this must be exciting,
as well.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the things about these
new "Star Wars" movies

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:33.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
is there's so many
strong female characters.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:34.427 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Is that really exciting

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.763
to be a part of this generation
of "Star Wars"?

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.764 line:92%
-It really is incredible.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.800 line:92%
And let's say, as a deep homage,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.838
we had the greatest muse
possible in Princess Leia,

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:47.207 line:92%
our beloved Carrie Fisher, so...

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:50.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]
Yes.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:55.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
So to continue that tradition
and have "Star Wars"

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the incredible producers
working on the film

00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:59.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Ryan Johnson
who wrote and directed it,

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:05.024
have these incredible female,
complicated, powerful women

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.059 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is really exciting.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.260 line:92%
-You mentioned "Jurassic Park."

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.064
Is that a film -- You say a lot
of people ask you about it.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that a film your children
have found,

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
and are they
impressed with that?

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:16.870 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh, I think so.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, my daughter
actually just saw it

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:22.041
for the first time at Halloween.
-Oh, wow.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.476 line:92%
-Her friends wanted to see it.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for years, she was like,
"Are you kidding?

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do not want to see my mother
being chased by a raptor.

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.783
That is not interesting to me."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.620
-You mean -- does she in general
play the cool card of

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.222 size:81% position:41%
"I'm not interested in
seeing mom in movies"?

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She's really interested
in movies.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:40.627
But me in jeopardy wasn't
deeply interesting to her.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
Oh, that's very sweet of her

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:45.231
that she didn't want to see you
get chased by dinosaurs.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:48.668
-But my son seemed fine with it.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.870 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Get her! Get her!"

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's like, "I feel like
one of the dinosaurs

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
would have caught you, Mom."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:58.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
"I've seen you run, girl."

00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:00.413 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But when she saw it,
was she happy?

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:03.516 line:92%
Did she think it was cool?

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:05.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She thought it was cool.
She loved it.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:07.520
And now they have both seen
"Star Wars" a few days ago,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.490
and I think they were really
excited by that too, so...

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.291 line:92%
-I think "Jurassic Park" --

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.726
and I know there is another one
of those coming as well,

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:16.262
which I'm sure you can't tell me
a word about,

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:16.930 size:75% position:38% line:92%
so I won't even ask.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:17.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can't tell you a word.
-Yeah.

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:20.633
But I will say, it still strikes
me that that moment of

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:23.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
seeing dinosaurs for the first
time in "Jurassic Park,"

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, what movies were
before that moment

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what movies were
after that moment

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:30.677
is one of those huge gaps that
in the theater, you realize --

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:31.578 line:92%
I still remember that awe.

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:35.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's incredible that
when we were making it,

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:35.982 size:78% position:39% line:92%
people now have said,

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:38.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Wow, being part of
a blockbuster,

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:39.018 line:92%
what did that feel like?"

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:44.490
But it felt like any other kind
of incredible, independent film,

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.392 line:92%
in that it was a pioneered film,

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:48.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
because CGI hadn't
really happened.

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:51.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-So Steven Spielberg was there

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:53.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
inventing with
these brilliant men,

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:57.303
like ILM and Sam Winston,
who did the animatronics,

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
like how to create
these creatures.

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:02.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was awe-inspiring.
-Yeah.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:05.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you were then
one of the first people

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:07.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
who had to as an actor
go like this...

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:08.181 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:09.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
-To something
that was not there.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:10.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly. Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:13.353 size:75% position:38%
The mouth-agape shot
from "Jurassic Park"

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:14.020 size:75% position:38% line:92%
has been seen a lot.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
People are like,
"Oh, my God, I love you.

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:18.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're the one that goes..."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:19.392 line:92%
-And it was probably just a guy

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:21.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
with, like, a tennis ball
and a stick.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:25.131
-Yes, it was an X
on a tennis ball. Exactly right.

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:27.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
Also scary.
-Yes, exactly.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:28.268 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But I think, again,

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:32.438
that is a credit to your
incredible talents as an actor.

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:32.972 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Very sweet.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am always so happy
to have you here.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:36.009 line:92%
Congratulations on the movie.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:38.678 size:84% position:42%
I can't wait to see you
at the Golden Globes.

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
Best of luck.
-Me too! Me too.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
Laura Dern, everybody.

